From 3305dcf80fac4059617286c373825351a4514104 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 08:56:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03592/11362] [outer-loop][prototype] Wire goal-ENERGY into
 plan_in_model (closes GAP-ARCH-GOAL-NOT-VERIFIED)

Worktree prototype (outer-loop/goal-energy), the synthesis's #1 highest-leverage move. The gap: the LLM
writes is_level_complete but it is graded by NOTHING, so a 99%-dynamics model with a wrong win-predicate
plans confidently to the wrong state. Wire exp4020's is_goal as a GRADED goal-energy the planner descends.

- induce_goal_energy(win_grids, non_win_grids) (arc_agi3_goal_induction): graded counterpart of
  induce_goal_predicate -- energy(grid)>=0, 0=goal satisfied, higher=violation magnitude (same object-count
  / colour hypotheses). Induced PER-GAME from the agent's OWN observed wins (not the frozen r11l asset --
  that is the silent-failure transfer risk the .426 directive flags); returns None with <2 wins.
- plan_in_model(goal_energy=...) (arc_executable_world_model): BEST-FIRST by goal-energy (descend toward the
  goal) instead of blind FIFO BFS. Backward-compatible (goal_energy=None keeps the exact original BFS).
- PROVEN (controlled remove-objects task): goal-energy reaches the win in 36 nodes vs blind BFS's 212 --
  5.9x FEWER nodes, same plan length, both win. 4 unit tests pass (incl. backward-compat).

HANDOFF for conductor productionization: wire per-game induction (from observed level-ups) into
graph_explore_solve_v2 / E3 plan_in_model calls + the MANDATORY ablation control + the silent-failure guard
(retire-as-universal + log verifier-gap if it fires wrongly on >=2 non-r11l games). Gate (per .426
known-issues): offline_reproduced=true on >=3 games with fewer actions-to-win than navigation-only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
